title: Who Controls the Treasury?
subtitle: Finance is a ministry, a veto point and KO's preferred border checkpoint.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_government_card
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and ministries_finalized = 1 and finance_minister_party = "Lewica" and month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_fiscal_policy_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_fiscal_policy_timer = 5
card-image: img/poland/cards/cost-programme.webp

= Who Controls the Treasury?

KO accepted a Left finance minister after harsh negotiations and now treats
every distributive decision as a test of whether that concession was a
mistake. The ministry's first real tax line will decide whether the office has
authority or merely a nameplate.

- @progressive_revenue
- @coalition_rule
- @publish_constraints

@progressive_revenue
title: Enforce a progressive revenue package
subtitle: Raise durable capacity and accept a hard liberal backlash.
on-arrival: budget += 2; fiscal_stress -= 3; workers_support += 4; progressive_credibility += 3; ko_coalition_dissent += 6; ko_relation -= 4; economic_growth -= 0.2; news_headline = "The Treasury shifts enforcement and relief toward a progressive tax settlement"

Capital income, top earners and aggressive avoidance move to the front of the
programme. The numbers work. KO's ministers respond by making clear that
arithmetical coherence is not the same thing as coalition consent.

- #poland_card_finish


@coalition_rule
title: Trade the package for a joint investment rule
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. A narrower settlement protects room for public investment.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Negotiating and defending a new fiscal rule requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; fiscal_stress -= 2; government_delivery += 3; ko_relation += 3; ko_coalition_dissent -= 2; budget_promises += 1; progressive_credibility -= 1; news_headline = "The coalition agrees a fiscal rule with protected investment space"

The Treasury gives up the headline confrontation in exchange for rules that
do not classify every hospital, railway and housing programme as identical
current spending. It is compromise with a ledger attached.

- #poland_card_finish


@publish_constraints
title: Publish the coalition's fiscal constraints
subtitle: No resource or budget cost. Keep the office and refuse to counterfeit agreement.
on-arrival: public_trust += 2; constitutional_restraint += 1; ko_relation += 1; government_delivery -= 1; progressives_dissent += 2; news_headline = "The Treasury publishes what the coalition will and will not finance"

No tax line changes today. Instead, the ministry releases the assumptions,
vetoes and trade-offs behind the budget. KO avoids a defeat; the Left avoids
pretending that a liberal ceiling is a law of nature.

- #poland_card_finish
